    <briefdescription>
<para>This structure contains the parameters for the Unique Device Endorsement (UDE) key provisioning command. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The UDE key pair (ECC NIST P-384) is generated inside the ASU (the private key never leaves the ASU), the private key is encrypted with the PUF KEK and programmed into the requested eFUSE slot, and a self-signed X.509 certificate over the generated public key is returned to the caller at CertBufAddr with its actual size at CertActualSizeAddr. </para>    </detaileddescription>
